{"note": "Facility levels observed turn by turn in one real Grand Concert career (Oguri Cap), transcribed from the screenshot capture of 2026-09-05. Source frames are 'Screenshot (N).png'. levels = [speed,stamina,power,guts,wit] as displayed on the training screen BEFORE that turn's training; null where the screen did not show them. 'selected' is the facility whose banner was open. Frames that were not training screens are recorded with selected:null and, where it was recoverable, an 'action' field (recreation / race / event). COVERAGE: frames 5-81, the whole career plus the URA finale. 55 in-career training turns carry a 'selected'.", "source": "screenshot-capture", "captured": "2026-09-05", "frameToTurn": "turn = (year-1)*24 + (month-1)*2 + (Early?1:2) for post-debut frames; pre-debut frames anchor frame 5 at turn 1. VERIFIED on 47 of 47 concertIn checks: turn + concertIn lands exactly on 24, 36, 48, 60 or 72 every time.", "summerCampWarning": "Turns 37-40 and 61-64 are summer camp. Camp forces the banner to read 'Lvl 5' for EVERY facility and hides the per-button level text, so rows with summerCamp:true carry levels:null and their selectedLevel of 5 is display, not a real level. Frame 43 shows 'Stamina Lvl 5' when stamina's true level is 1. Camp trainings also do NOT advance the 1+floor(uses/4) level counter -- the wit 4->5 window (turns 29,30,[37 camp],43,44 -> shows at 45) only comes out to four uses if the camp one is excluded.", "readingHazard": "Sparkle/glow overlays on the SELECTED facility's button corrupt the level digit at full-frame resolution. Frame 47's Speed reads as 5 and is a 3. Cross-check the banner against the button against the next frame before recording a level-up.", "transcribed": "frames 5-42 on 2026-09-11; frames 43-81 on 2026-09-12"}
